  "label": "TMUA 2022 · Paper 2 · Question 2",
  "lead": "<img class=\"source-question\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Enlarge question\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"TMUA 2022 · Paper 2 · Question 2 — Find the coefficient of x⁵ in (1+x)⁵(1+x+…+x⁵).\">",
  "options": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D",
    "E"
  ],
  "correct": "E",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Collect matching powers",
      "body": "<p>In a product of two polynomials, a term from the first factor and a term from the second contribute to the requested coefficient when their exponents add to the target exponent.</p>",
      "recap": "Multiply coefficients within each matching pair, then add the contributions.",
      "pitfall": "Reading only the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> term from one factor misses the cross terms.",
      "pause": "List every matching pair of powers, work out their coefficients, and add them.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b2-l05",
          "reminder": "Coefficients in a product come from every pair of powers with the target total."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>To obtain <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x02026;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>, pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math> in the first factor with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math> in the second for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mi>&#x02026;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>. The second coefficient is always 1.</p><p>The required coefficient is the complete sum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>&#x02026;</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer E: 32.</strong></p>",
